# Drive one loaded-session turn so a run that carries the
# INCURSION_MUSIC_CHOIR_PROBE probe counts as gameplay. The probe itself
# runs on entry to Game::Play, before any key is read, so nothing in this
# script steers the probe. Two things still have to happen.
#
# First, the probe's own two casts of "Music of the Spheres" each print a
# message long enough to trip the engine's "-- more --" page break
# (TextTerm::Message, src/TextTerm.cpp:352), which blocks on a keystroke.
# That is the key the old single 's' was eaten by: the first prompt ate it
# and the second found the script exhausted, so the session ended before
# the probe's errors.log lines were ever flushed. SPACE clears a prompt
# (any key but a direction does), so SPACE*80 sits well above the handful
# of prompts two casts can raise; ESC*20 follows as the line-of-fire
# keys' own belt-and-braces (tools/keys/line-of-fire.keys).
#
# Second, once the prompts are cleared the session must complete at least
# one real turn, or tools/headless.sh reports NO GAMEPLAY. 's' is search:
# one completed turn, which is all the NO GAMEPLAY guard wants. @quit then
# ends the session cleanly (SK_QUIT, src/Wposix.cpp). No @expect/@dump:
# this script has no screen to read, its oracle is logs/errors.log written
# by the probe.
#
#   INCURSION_MUSIC_CHOIR_PROBE=1 \
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/xsummon-priest-seed5-opt0822.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/music-choir.keys 1
#
# The character is loaded, not built: a key-built character moves when lib/
# resource ids move (tools/fixtures/README.md), and this check asserts exact
# damage numbers read off that character's caster level.

SPACE*80
ESC*20

s

@quit
